            <ArticleTitle>Cocaine-associated chest pain in a chest pain center.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>394-6, A10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chest pain is the most common cocaine-related complaint. The objective of this study was to describe an emergency department-based chest pain center for patients with cocaine-associated chest pain and to evaluate the safety of this protocol by assessing cardiac complications at 30 days.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
